From 2bc6507077aabc6a198bb6773945f40ae6d726da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:59:49 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Home: Friday theater releases get their own row; six
 headlines beside the lead

Concept C from the November 6 middle-band review. On Fridays the theater
releases were the tallest block in the front's side column (a poster and a
tickets button per film), leaving the lead and More headlines columns
half-empty. They now sit in their own full-width row between the front and
More from today, using the existing five-across poster grid (three across on
tablets). More headlines shows six stories instead of four, so the centre
reaches the height of Today & Tonight. Phones are unchanged.

The side-column overrides that squeezed the poster grid into a list are
removed from broadsheet.css and tablet.css. home-columns now checks the
releases sit below the front at full width and never inside its columns.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
